      "response": {
        "question": "How do scanlation groups work?",
        "answer": "Scanlation groups are fan‑run collectives that digitise, translate, clean, typeset and quality‑check manga or manhwa chapters. They split the work into roles such as raw providers, translators, cleaners, typesetters and quality checkers, coordinate via the internet—often using IRC or Discord—and publish the finished chapters on their own websites or image‑hosting services. The work is usually done without permission from the copyright holder.",
